      "message": {
        "author": {
          "name": null,
          "role": "assistant"
        },
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "\ue200image_group\ue202{\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"query\":[\"planting seeds garden hands soil spring\",\"child learning gardening with parent\",\"watering plants sunlight growth garden\",\"small garden sprouts early spring\"],\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\nThere\u2019s something about planting a garden that feels like starting over\u2026 in the best way.\n\nThis season, I\u2019m not just putting seeds into the ground, I\u2019m planting pieces of a new life. Fresh soil, fresh air, fresh eyes on everything around me. Slowing down enough to notice the sunlight hitting the leaves, the quiet growth happening beneath the surface, the little moments that used to pass me by.\n\nWe\u2019re building something from the ground up\u2026 together.\n\nWatching my son learn has been my favorite part. His excitement, his curiosity, his tiny hands digging into the dirt like it\u2019s the most important job in the world. But even more than that\u2026 it\u2019s watching the man beside him.\n\nThe way he takes his time.  \nThe patience.  \nThe kindness.  \nThe intention behind every word he pours into him.\n\nThat\u2019s what stays with me.\n\nBecause while we\u2019re planting seeds in the garden\u2026 he\u2019s planting seeds in my son.  \nSeeds of confidence.  \nOf strength.  \nOf what it means to lead with love.\n\nAnd I know those will grow far beyond anything we harvest.\n\nSpring has always been about new beginnings\u2026 but this one feels different. It feels real. It feels rooted. It feels like growth I can actually see and touch and hold onto.\n\nRight now, life feels like watering something beautiful and trusting it will bloom.\n\nAnd honestly\u2026 I\u2019ve never felt more at peace watching things grow \ud83c\udf31"
          ]
        },
